--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACTION REQUIRED BEFORE DISTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The verbatim RPL-1.5 text has NOT been vendored into this file. It must be
pasted here, unmodified, from the canonical source above before this software is
distributed or offered as a service.

Why this file exists in this state: DEC-13 accepted RPL-1.5 as a consequence of
depending on MediatR 14.2.0, which is licensed RPL-1.5 or commercially. The
obligation is recorded so it cannot be forgotten; the text is not reproduced from
memory, because a licence quoted approximately is worse than one quoted by
reference.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS LICENCE REQUIRES OF YOU
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

RPL-1.5 differs from ordinary copyleft in one way that matters here: the
reciprocal obligation attaches on DEPLOYMENT AS A SERVICE, not only on shipping
binaries. If this API is hosted for third parties rather than run internally, the
source of this codebase -- not merely modifications to MediatR -- must be made
available to them under compatible terms.

Two consequences follow, both recorded in DEC-13:

  1. Anything committed to this repository, including its history, is
     publishable by obligation. Committed credentials are therefore a
     disclosure, not untidiness.

  2. Closing the source later requires revisiting DEC-13 and either purchasing
     the Lucky Penny commercial licence, pinning MediatR to 12.5.0 (Apache-2.0,
     the last permissively licensed release), or replacing MediatR with a
     hand-rolled dispatcher.

See docs/architecture/design.md, DEC-13.
